        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "A mixture of acetylacetone (Hacac, 1.0 mmol) and triethylamine (1.5 mmol) was added dropwise to a methanolic solution of DyCl3·xH2O (0.5 mmol, 188 mg) under ambient air/moisture. After 15 min of stirring, the clear colorless mixture was filtered and the filtrate was left undisturbed at room temperature. After 5 days, yellow block-shaped single crystals of 1 formed as the minor product together with colorless needles of Dy(acac)3·2H2O (major product) and were separated under an optical microscope.",
